p` and you get two directories: `basin_dataset_public` and `basin_dataset_public_v1p2`. The directory `basin_dataset_public` is mostly empty, without readme files, and should be deleted.\r\n1. It is not immediately obvious where to find the description of data files. It could help to move all README files except `readme_FIRST.txt` to a `docs` directory\r\n1. The first 10 lines of `dataset_summary.txt` are repeated.\r\n1. I think that you need a short description of the file structure in `readme_FIRST.txt`\r\n1. In `readme_FIRST.txt` you say `Hour is set to zero since these are daily values` in `readme_basin_mean_forcing.txt` -- but in the daymet files this is set to 12. It could be useful to say what the hour represents -- e.g., forcing data for the previous 24 hours?\r\n1. It is cumbersome to navigate through the files. You will need to use file `gauge_information.txt` to identify the different files (directory and file name) and then other files `basin_physical_characteristics.txt` for additional information. Quite a bit of searching was required to even find `gauge_information.txt`","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NCAR/CAMELS/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NCAR/CAMELS/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}